is property investing dead it's  september  2021 and property prices have absolutely  rocketed all across the country and in  many parts of the world now as property  prices go up that actually means that  it's harder for investors and first-time  buyers to get the deposit together to  buy a property  as a buy to let investor the higher  prices are then that means that your  deposit is higher also stamp duty  holiday has now ended so the amount of  money that you have to put down to buy  an average house is significantly higher  than it was a few years ago  that being said it's much harder to get  the returns that you could get back in  the day especially with things like the  tenants rights tenants now if there's a  bad tenant to get rid of them is a  process it's expensive and then you've  also got problems like the tax changes  section 24 that have meant that you  can't claim your mortgage expense back  as tax deductible unless you buy through  a company which of course means that you  have to pay an accountant to do your  accounts so is the profit being squeezed  out of buy to let property so much so  that it doesn't make sense anymore to  save deposits and buy a property and  build a portfolio well my thinking is  whenever the market changes you need to  be creative and you need to find new  ways to win in property buy to let  vanilla straight forward buy to let is  less attractive than it was  five ten fifteen years ago i first  bought my first bite property in 2009  it's now 2021. there's a lot of changes  house prices have doubled in value in  most parts of the country so what is the  solution how can property as a vehicle  continue to be  productive  profitable and how can you recycle your  deposits and get more for your money  wow  what i think property investors should  start looking at now instead of buying a  property with the view to rent the  property out and get a high return or a  high yield i think it's much more  lucrative if you can find properties  instead of finding properties that would  make good rentals  is to find properties that have got  something wrong with them  find a rundown property that's  unmortgageable or maybe there's no  kitchen there's no bathroom if there's  no kitchen or bathroom in a property you  cannot get a mortgage on that property  so all the buy to let investors all the  first-time buyers  cannot compete with these rundown  problem properties  how are you going to compete then how  are you going to buy these properties  well what you're going to do is you're  going to instead of getting a mortgage  you're gonna buy them with a bridging  loan  now some people are scared about  bridging loans because they're expensive  they've not done them before they're  afraid of the unknown however when you  know what you're doing bridging loans  can be a very good tool  so  let's say you find a rundown property  let's say you agree to buy it nice and  cheap and you buy it with a bridging  loan instead of a mortgage you're still  going to need a deposit you're going to  use a bridging loan this property is now  effectively as far as the seller is  concerned it's a cash purchase there's  no mortgage bridging is expensive but  it's also very very quick this also  opens you up to auction properties and  all of the rundown nasty properties that  nobody's interested in and nobody can  compete with because they need a  mortgage to buy their properties  once you've bought these rundown problem  properties what are you going to do are  you going to rent them out well you  can't because they're in such bad  condition  so what you're going to do is you're  going to fix these properties up you're  going to get a new kitchen a new  bathroom you're gonna if there's a  structural problem you're gonna fix it  once you've done this you've pushed the  value of the property up  now you'll find that the property is  mortgageable which means that it's  suddenly going to be achievable a much  higher price for that property  you're going to then take out a mortgage  and the mortgage is going to pay back  the bridging company and in some cases  it's going to pay you back more than the  bridging loan and you will get your  deposit back in full  then you can rent the property out  you've got your deposit back to go again  and again and again this strategy you've  probably heard of as the buy refurbish  refinance rent it means you can recycle  the small money you have instead of  leaving it down as a deposit on a buy to  let property mean you can recycle your  money and build a larger portfolio  making more profit and this is the new  way of investing in 2021.  if you'd like to see an example of this  done i'd highly recommend that you watch  a documentary that i made where i showed  you the a to z  of finding buying refurbing refinancing  a property i show you me doing this with  one of my properties up north in  darlington and if you'd like to watch  that video i'm going to leave it right  up here for you to watch please also do  like the video if you enjoyed this and  don't forget to subscribe and i'll see  you on the next video
 

